# Working documents for the submission itself, not artifacts of the project. They carry notes
# written for us rather than for a reader - what to fix before recording, what to say on camera,
# which forms are worth filing - and this repo is linked publicly from the Devpost entry.
# README.md and SETUP.md are the docs a visitor should actually find.
DEVPOST.md
DEMO_SCRIPT.md
DEPLOY.md

### Frontend build output ###
# `npm run build` writes the compiled React app here so `mvn package` bundles it into the jar.
# It is generated, so it stays out of git: committing a minified bundle guarantees merge
# conflicts every time two people touch the frontend. Build before packaging - see DEPLOY.md.
src/main/resources/static/
SETUP.md
